[2026-03-15T23:45:09.328Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GZt4uzx2JeZRYbUzovY5Bi","type":"tool_result","content":"    40→You MUST read these skill files before testing.\n    41→\n    42→https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md\n    43→https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md\n    44→\n    45→RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY is already set in the environment for using the Replay CLI.\n    46→\n    47→## Replay.io Playwright Installation and Configuration\n    48→\n    49→Every app MUST use the Replay browser to record Playwright test runs. This section describes\n    50→the exact installation steps and configuration required.\n    51→\n    52→### 1. Install dependencies\n    53→\n    54→The app's `package.json` must include these dev dependencies:\n    55→\n    56→```bash\n    57→npm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright @playwright/test\n    58→```\n    59→\n    60→`@replayio/playwright` (currently v5.0.1) provides the `replayReporter` and `devices` exports\n    61→for integrating Replay recordings into Playwright.\n    62→\n    63→### 2. Install the Replay browser\n    64→\n    65→Run once in the container (or as part of CI setup):\n    66→\n    67→```bash\n    68→npx replayio install\n    69→```\n    70→\n    71→This downloads the Replay Chromium browser to `~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome`.\n    72→Verify it exists:\n    73→\n    74→```bash\n    75→ls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome\n    76→```\n    77→\n    78→### 3. API key\n    79→\n    80→`RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` must be set in the environment. It is already available in this\n    81→container. The Playwright config passes it to the reporter via:\n    82→\n    83→```ts\n    84→apiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→### 4. Playwright config\n    88→\n    89→The Playwright config MUST:\n    90→\n    91→1. Import BOTH `replayReporter` and `devices as replayDevices` from `@replayio/playwright`.\n    92→2. Include `replayReporter(...)` in the `reporter` array with `upload: false`. Uploads are\n    93→   handled by the test script, NOT by the reporter.\n    94→3. Spread `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']` into the global `use` config. This sets\n    95→   `executablePath`, `RECORD_ALL_CONTENT`, and critically `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE` which\n    96→   is required for the reporter to attach test metadata (pass/fail result) to recordings.\n    97→   Without `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`, the recording driver cannot read the per-test\n    98→   metadata written by the fixture, and all recordings will have empty `testResult`.\n    99→\n   100→**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT manually set `launchOptions.executablePath` and `env` instead of using\n   101→`replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`. Manual config misses `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`,\n   102→which breaks the recording-to-test metadata association.\n   103→\n   104→**IMPORTANT**: The Replay Chromium browser adds instrumentation overhead that makes all\n   105→operations ~2–3x slower than standard Chromium. Always set higher timeouts from the start:\n   106→\n   107→- `actionTimeout: 15000` (15s for clicks, fills, etc.)\n   108→- `navigationTimeout: 30000` (30s for page navigations)\n   109→- Use `expect.toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 })` for post-navigation assertions\n   110→\n   111→Example:\n   112→\n   113→```ts\n   114→import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';\n   115→import { devices as replayDevices, replayReporter } from '@replayio/playwright';\n   116→\n   117→export default defineConfig({\n   118→  // Replay Chromium is slower due to instrumentation — use generous timeouts\n   119→  actionTimeout: 15000,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4c6f06f-287c-4f14-81da-eb182281b13a","uuid":"647a88e2-4aee-41d9-8448-7a417f7ca9e5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/tasks/build/testing.md","content":"You MUST read these skill files before testing.\n\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md\nhttps://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md\n\nRECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY is already set in the environment for using the Replay CLI.\n\n## Replay.io Playwright Installation and Configuration\n\nEvery app MUST use the Replay browser to record Playwright test runs. This section describes\nthe exact installation steps and configuration required.\n\n### 1. Install dependencies\n\nThe app's `package.json` must include these dev dependencies:\n\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev @replayio/playwright @playwright/test\n```\n\n`@replayio/playwright` (currently v5.0.1) provides the `replayReporter` and `devices` exports\nfor integrating Replay recordings into Playwright.\n\n### 2. Install the Replay browser\n\nRun once in the container (or as part of CI setup):\n\n```bash\nnpx replayio install\n```\n\nThis downloads the Replay Chromium browser to `~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome`.\nVerify it exists:\n\n```bash\nls ~/.replay/runtimes/chrome-linux/chrome\n```\n\n### 3. API key\n\n`RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` must be set in the environment. It is already available in this\ncontainer. The Playwright config passes it to the reporter via:\n\n```ts\napiKey: process.env.REPLAY_API_KEY ?? process.env.RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY\n```\n\n### 4. Playwright config\n\nThe Playwright config MUST:\n\n1. Import BOTH `replayReporter` and `devices as replayDevices` from `@replayio/playwright`.\n2. Include `replayReporter(...)` in the `reporter` array with `upload: false`. Uploads are\n   handled by the test script, NOT by the reporter.\n3. Spread `replayDevices['Replay Chromium']` into the global `use` config. This sets\n   `executablePath`, `RECORD_ALL_CONTENT`, and critically `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE` which\n   is required for the reporter to attach test metadata (pass/fail result) to recordings.\n   Without `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`, the recording driver cannot read the per-test\n   metadata written by the fixture, and all recordings will have empty `testResult`.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT manually set `launchOptions.executablePath` and `env` instead of using\n`replayDevices['Replay Chromium']`. Manual config misses `RECORD_REPLAY_METADATA_FILE`,\nwhich breaks the recording-to-test metadata association.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The Replay Chromium browser adds instrumentation overhead that makes all\noperations ~2–3x slower than standard Chromium. Always set higher timeouts from the start:\n\n- `actionTimeout: 15000` (15s for clicks, fills, etc.)\n- `navigationTimeout: 30000` (30s for page navigations)\n- Use `expect.toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 })` for post-navigation assertions\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';\nimport { devices as replayDevices, replayReporter } from '@replayio/playwright';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  // Replay Chromium is slower due to instrumentation — use generous timeouts\n  actionTimeout: 15000,","numLines":80,"startLine":40,"totalLines":944}}}
