ndering if the Neon endpoint is going dormant during the reseeding process, or if the endpoint used by the Netlify functions is actually different from the one the tests are connecting to. There's also a cleanup function that runs after all tests complete, which might be relevant to understanding the full lifecycle here.\n\nLet me reconsider the actual problem—maybe the DATABASE_URL environment variable isn't being read correctly by the Netlify functions when running with the `--offline` flag, which would explain why all the tests are hitting \"Property not found\" errors. The test script's beforeAll fails for test 4 because the Neon endpoint got suspended, but the functions are failing silently and returning 404s instead.\n\nLooking at the Neon error more carefully—\"The requested endpoint could not be found\" suggests the endpoint doesn't exist anymore, not that it's suspended. The cleanup step in the test script deletes branches matching \"test-run-\", so there might be a race condition where the current branch is getting deleted by a previous run before the tests finish.\n\nBut wait, tests 1-3 passed their beforeAll without throwing errors, yet they're showing \"property not found\" errors. That suggests the beforeAll seeded successfully for those tests, but the API is somehow using a different DATABASE_URL than what's in the .env file. The test script writes DATABASE_URL to .env and netlify dev should read it, but if netlify dev was already running from a reused server, it might be holding onto an old environment. Even though the test script kills the server in step 1, maybe that kill didn't fully work and an old instance is still running with stale credentials.\n\nLet me check the property detail page component to see if there's something wrong with how it's rendering.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3443,"cache_read_input_tokens":65990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_token